tmux.repl - a two-pane command REPL in tmux

Usage:
  tmux.repl start [SESSION]   Start or attach to a REPL session
  tmux.repl stop [SESSION]    Stop a session and remove its state
  tmux.repl --help            Show this help

The left pane runs the Reply-based input frontend directly. The right pane runs
tmux.show directly. tmux.repl.input is a separate PTY worker process. Commands,
output events, and exit statuses travel over per-session durable LavinMQ streams.

When started with a custom interactive command, its pane output is captured to
the session log and tmux.show follows that log.

Environment:
  TMUX_REPL_SESSION          Default session name
  XDG_STATE_HOME             State directory base
  LAVINMQ_AMQP_UNIXSOCKET    Required LavinMQ AMQP Unix socket

Requires tmux, tmux.repl, tmux.repl.input, tmux.show, and LavinMQ.
